<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Use Case Specification - UC-16</title>
<style>
  body {
    font-family: 'Calibri', 'Segoe UI', Arial, sans-serif;
    margin: 40px;
    line-height: 1.4;
    font-size: 11pt;
  }
  h2 {
    text-align: center;
    font-family: 'Calibri', sans-serif;
    font-weight: bold;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  table {
    border-collapse: collapse;
    width: 100%;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  td {
    border: 1px solid #000000;
    padding: 8px 12px;
    vertical-align: top;
    font-size: 10pt;
  }
  .label-cell {
    font-weight: bold;
    width: 20%;
    background-color: #F3F4F6;
  }
  .header-title {
    background-color: #E5E7EB;
    font-weight: bold;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 14pt;
    padding: 10px;
  }
  .flow-list {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 20px;
  }
  .flow-list li {
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .sub-list {
    margin-top: 4px;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
    padding-left: 20px;
    list-style-type: lower-alpha;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

  <h2>Use Case Specification</h2>

  <table>
    <tbody>
      <!-- Title Row -->
      <tr>
        <td colspan="4" class="header-title">UC-16: View Round Leaderboard / Rankings</td>
      </tr>
      
      <!-- Created Info -->
      <tr>
        <td class="label-cell" style="width:15%;">Created By:</td>
        <td style="width:35%;">Nguyen Khoi Nguyen</td>
        <td class="label-cell" style="width:15%;">Date Created:</td>
        <td style="width:35%;">2026-06-16</td>
      </tr>
      
      <!-- Actors -->
      <tr>
        <td class="label-cell">Primary Actor:</td>
        <td>Public / Guest (Khách vãng lai)</td>
        <td class="label-cell">Secondary Actors:</td>
        <td>None</td>
      </tr>
      
      <!-- Trigger -->
      <tr>
        <td class="label-cell" colspan="1">Trigger:</td>
        <td colspan="3">A user visits the Hackathon public web portal and clicks on the "Leaderboard" or "Rankings" section.</td>
      </tr>
      
      <!-- Description -->
      <tr>
        <td class="label-cell" colspan="1">Description:</td>
        <td colspan="3">The "View Round Leaderboard / Rankings" use case describes the process by which any user, including unauthenticated guests, can view the real-time rankings and scores of teams participating in a specific round of a hackathon.</td>
      </tr>
      
      <!-- Preconditions -->
      <tr>
        <td class="label-cell" colspan="1">Preconditions:</td>
        <td colspan="3">
          <ul class="flow-list">
            <li><b>PRE-1:</b> The Hackathon event has started and has at least one active or completed round.</li>
            <li><b>PRE-2:</b> Leaderboard visibility is enabled by the Organizer (or scores are published).</li>
          </ul>
        </td>
      </tr>
      
      <!-- Post-conditions -->
      <tr>
        <td class="label-cell" colspan="1">Post-conditions:</td>
        <td colspan="3">
          <ul class="flow-list">
            <li><b>POST-1:</b> The system successfully renders the real-time leaderboard table showing team positions, names, and total scores to the user.</li>
          </ul>
        </td>
      </tr>
      
      <!-- Normal Flow -->
      <tr>
        <td class="label-cell" colspan="1">Normal Flow:</td>
        <td colspan="3">
          <ol class="flow-list">
            <li>The user visits the public Hackathon portal.</li>
            <li>The user navigates to the "Leaderboard / Rankings" tab.</li>
            <li>The system displays a dropdown list of active Hackathon events and their rounds.</li>
            <li>The user selects a specific Hackathon event and the desired Round.</li>
            <li>The system queries the database to retrieve the latest team scores and calculated rankings for the selected round <b>[see 1-EF]</b>.</li>
            <li>The system sorts the teams in descending order based on their total scores.</li>
            <li>The system displays the leaderboard containing: Rank, Team Name, Member Count, Total Score, and Submission Status.</li>
            <li>The user can type a team name in the search bar to filter the leaderboard results <b>[see 1-AF]</b>.</li>
          </ol>
        </td>
      </tr>
      
      <!-- Alternative Flows -->
      <tr>
        <td class="label-cell" colspan="1">Alternative Flows:</td>
        <td colspan="3">
          <p style="margin:0 0 6px 0;"><b>1-AF: Search query returns no results</b></p>
          <ul class="flow-list" style="list-style-type:none; padding-left:10px;">
            <li>a. The user enters a search term that doesn't match any team name.</li>
            <li>b. The system displays a notice: "No teams found matching your search query."</li>
            <li>c. The system displays an empty table and allows the user to clear or edit the search query.</li>
            <li>d. The use case continues from step 7 of the Normal Flow.</li>
          </ul>
        </td>
      </tr>
      
      <!-- Exceptions -->
      <tr>
        <td class="label-cell" colspan="1">Exceptions:</td>
        <td colspan="3">
          <p style="margin:0 0 6px 0;"><b>1-EF: Database query failure</b></p>
          <ul class="flow-list" style="list-style-type:none; padding-left:10px;">
            <li>1. The system fails to retrieve the ranking details from the database.</li>
            <li>2. The system displays an error message: "Failed to load rankings. Please refresh the page or try again later."</li>
            <li>3. The use case terminates.</li>
          </ul>
        </td>
      </tr>
      
      <!-- Priority & Frequency -->
      <tr>
        <td class="label-cell" style="width:15%;">Priority:</td>
        <td style="width:35%;">Medium</td>
        <td class="label-cell" style="width:15%;">Frequency of Use:</td>
        <td style="width:35%;">High (Constantly requested by public users during hackathons)</td>
      </tr>
      
      <!-- Business Rules -->
      <tr>
        <td class="label-cell" colspan="1">Business Rules:</td>
        <td colspan="3">
          <ul class="flow-list">
            <li><b>BR-1: Open Access:</b> No authentication or user account is required to access the leaderboard.</li>
            <li><b>BR-2: Real-time Calculation:</b> Rankings are dynamically updated based on the latest approved grades submitted by judges.</li>
            <li><b>BR-3: Visibility Window:</b> The Organizer can choose to hide or publish the leaderboard for specific rounds (e.g., hiding scores during a final pitch event).</li>
          </ul>
        </td>
      </tr>
      
      <!-- Other Information -->
      <tr>
        <td class="label-cell" colspan="1">Other Information:</td>
        <td colspan="3">
          None.
        </td>
      </tr>
      
      <!-- Assumptions -->
      <tr>
        <td class="label-cell" colspan="1">Assumptions:</td>
        <td colspan="3">
          <ul class="flow-list">
            <li>The system can handle a high volume of concurrent read requests to the leaderboard without database lockups.</li>
            <li>Judges submit scores in a timely manner, allowing the leaderboard to reflect active progress.</li>
          </ul>
        </td>
      </tr>
      
    </tbody>
  </table>

</body>
</html>
